Why Is Demand Increasing
Data Center Expansion: Hyperscale and enterprise data centers are increasing purchases of DRAM modules and enterprise SSDs as digital workloads continue to expand.
AI Server Growth: AI and machine-learning workloads require substantially higher memory capacity and bandwidth, accelerating demand for advanced server memory solutions.
DDR5 and High-Speed Storage: Migration toward DDR5, NVMe SSDs, and PCIe Gen4/Gen5 interfaces is increasing performance requirements across modern server architectures.

Data Center Memory Watch: High-Capacity and Energy-Efficient Solutions
Server memory development is increasingly focused on higher bandwidth, greater capacity, energy efficiency, and new architectures. CXL memory expansion, persistent memory, ruggedized edge-server solutions, and memory-centric computing are emerging as areas of technology development as enterprises and cloud operators seek to improve infrastructure utilization.

